  "text": "Children with bipolar disorder sometimes feel very happy or “up” and are much more energetic and active than usual. This is called a manic episode . Children with bipolar disorder sometimes feel very sad or “down” and are much less active than usual. This is called a depressive episode . Bipolar disorder is often episodic, but it usually lasts a lifetime.",
